<p>Note 1: The above pro forma net income for the 1997 periods included non-recurring costs associated with certain 1997 pooling of interest transactions of $231 and $348 related to acquisitions for the three and six months ended June 30, 1997 respectively.  Excluding costs, pro forma net income before extraordinary item would have been $8,951 and  10,668 and pro forma EPS would have been $0.45 and $0.54 for the three months and six months ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>The extraordinary items for the three months and six months are the result of  the early extinguishment of debt at several companies.</p>
<p>Note 2: On May 17, 1996, Coach USA acquired six motorcoach businesses (the &quot;Founding Companies&quot;), simultaneously with the closing of its initial public offering. The above pro forma data reflects the results of the Founding Companies and Pooled Companies combined as of January 1, 1996, and the Purchased Companies from their date of acquisition.</p>
<p>Note 3: Prior to the mergers, the Founding and Pooled Companies have been managed as independent private companies. In conjunction with the mergers, certain stockholders have agreed to reductions in salaries and benefits and have entered into employment agreements.</p>
